title: 'Studio Recipe Phase 1 shipped — value-play scaffolded, both pipelines recipe-aware'
summary: 'Implemented Studio Recipe Phase 1 end-to-end the same day the spec was written. Two commits, no new npm dependencies, 18 new tests added (115/115 in CLI, 578/578 across the workspace — every package green). Studio Recipe is now a first-class concept in Atelier: the StudioRecipe interface ships in @a-company/atelier-types alongside SilencePolicy/CaptionStyle/CaptionGrouping; StudioRecipeSchema + validateRecipe ship in @a-company/atelier-schema (reserved-field warnings included so Phase 1 authors aren''t blindsided when Phase 3 ships); the recipe.ts lib in CLI provides loadRecipe / scaffoldRecipeYaml / three applyRecipeTo* translation functions / renderRecipeWithDefaults / recipeToYaml. Four new CLI verbs: atelier recipe new / validate / show, and atelier apply-recipe <project> <recipe> as the convenience chain. The --recipe flag was threaded into atelier trim, atelier transcribe, and atelier captions regenerate; TrimOptions gained matchTolerance and TranscribeOptions gained captionOptions to carry recipe values through to the underlying pipelines. CLI options always win over recipe per the spec §4.1 precedence decision. Partial recipes are valid — any omitted field falls back to its code default. Reserved Phase 3 fields (overlay_rules, caption_highlight, transition_kit, palette, audio_policy, aspect_targets) parse as opaque so Phase 1 recipes remain forward-compatible. End-to-end dogfood pass: scaffold a recipe, validate it, see PASS with zero warnings, demonstrating the path works on a clean machine.'
