learnings:
  - 'The three-layer ship-pattern (foundation → core → surface) compressed to two commits here because the foundation (types + schema) and core (translation lib) were tightly coupled by the option-threading changes in TrimOptions/TranscribeOptions. Either could ship as the next feature''s prerequisite, but together they form an indivisible "make the pipelines recipe-aware" change.'
  - 'CLI-wins precedence (§4.1) is implemented as "fill in from recipe ONLY where CLI didn''t specify" — `cliOptions.padPre ?? policy.default_padding_pre`. This means a user can scratch-build a recipe from their own --pad-pre experiments and have it survive future invocations.'
  - 'Reserved-field warnings are load-time, not validate-only. Every loadRecipe call returns warnings; CLI verbs surface them. Authors see them even if they never run `recipe validate` explicitly. This is the right default — silent reserved fields would create surprise when Phase 3 ships.'
  - 'scaffoldRecipeYaml emits a heavily-commented YAML with inline field explanations. The starter doc IS the docs for someone editing their first recipe. Discoverability over file cleanliness — chose intentionally per spec §10 open question.'
  - 'Path resolution chain (project-local → ~/.atelier/recipes/ → literal path) is symmetric with how shell PATH resolution works. Users with a personal library can `--recipe my-style` from any project without paths. Project-specific overrides win because they live in source control alongside the project.'
  - 'Translation functions (applyRecipeTo*) live in lib/recipe.ts, NOT duplicated per command. This is the spec §13 "centralize all recipe→options logic" risk mitigation. Future commands that gain --recipe just import the relevant transform; no chance of drift.'
  - 'The captionOptions threading via TranscribeOptions.captionOptions: BuildCaptionsOptions is the integration point between the recipe layer and the runtime caption builder. Importantly, captionOptions is optional — when present (from a recipe) it merges with the builder''s DEFAULT_STYLE inside buildCaptionLayers; when absent (no recipe) the builder uses its own defaults. Clean.'
  - 'Phase 3 deferral is preserved at the type level (unknown) AND the schema level (z.unknown()). When Phase 3 ships, we tighten both in lockstep, and any Phase 1 recipe that happened to declare a reserved field becomes meaningful. validateRecipe will lose its warning for that field on that recipe version bump. This is the right migration path.'
  - 'Zero new dependencies across all three video Phase 2 features (T-007b, T-006, Studio Recipe). This is the dividend of the subprocess-only / Zod / yaml discipline established at the start. Each pure-function lib was unit-testable in isolation without mocking.'
